  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund: Using EO technology to improve production of agriculture statistics in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to further modernise Rwanda&#x2019;s agricultural statistics by incorporating Earth Observation (EO) techniques and Machine Learning. Building on the UK-Rwanda partnership in statistics, the UK Office for National Statistics (ONS) will support the National Institute of Statistics of Rwanda (NISR) in integrating modern technologies into existing frameworks, producing high-quality, timely data for evidence-based decision-making.
This project will focus specifically on agricultural statistics, an area that remains underdeveloped. The British High Commission in Kigali intends to convene experts and key stakeholders to explore best practices for using earth observation techniques and machine learning to complement traditional agriculture statistics obtained through surveys.</narrative>
  </description>
